Hiring Team \
Oregon Primary Care Association

Dear Hiring Team,

I'm applying for the Data & Application Support Analyst 1 role. What draws me to it is how directly it combines two things I've already spent time on separately: pulling together data that actually informs a program, and sitting with the people that data is about while they tell you what's working and what isn't. This role puts both in the same job, in service of health centers that need someone reliable on the other end of a support request.

At Future Generations Collaborative, I worked alongside Health Share Oregon on community feedback and data collection tied to their programs. I sat in on program-improvement meetings and helped facilitate a community forum where Health Share Oregon staff came in and heard directly from the community they serve. That work taught me that data is only useful once someone has actually listened to the people it describes, and that the follow-through — showing up to the next meeting, checking that feedback landed somewhere — matters as much as the collection itself. I also supported yearly grant reporting and data collection for that same partnership, so I've done the more routine side of this work too.

The application-support half of the role is familiar from a different angle. I built a tool that turns spoken inventory counts into clean, usable data using SQL and Python, and put it directly into the hands of bar staff at Soho House. When something broke or didn't match how they actually worked, I fixed it and added what they needed. That loop of build, hand it to a real user, listen, adjust is the same one this role runs with health centers instead of bartenders.

I don't have hands-on experience yet with Arcadia or VisualizOR specifically, but I pick up new platforms quickly, and I'd rather be upfront about that than overstate it. What I can offer immediately is careful data handling, a service-oriented approach built from years of direct customer support, and firsthand experience with the kind of community feedback loop this role exists to support.

Thank you for considering my application. I'd welcome the chance to talk about how this experience could support OPCA's member health centers.

Sincerely, \
Matt Loera
